{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/amplitudeencoding\/amplitudebatchencoder"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"abstract":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" of Amplitude’s HTTP V2 API, so an ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" can","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"send events to an Amplitude project’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"POST \/2\/httpapi","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeBatchEncoder","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"AmplitudeEncoding"}],"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeBatchEncoder.swift#L74","fileName":"AmplitudeBatchEncoder.swift"},"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AmplitudeBatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"AmplitudeBatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}],"externalID":"s:17AmplitudeEncoding0A12BatchEncoderV","title":"AmplitudeBatchEncoder","symbolKind":"struct","roleHeading":"Structure"},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeBatchEncoder\/init(apiKey:plan:limit:)"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Initializers","title":"Initializers"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Methods","title":"Instance Methods"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeBatchEncoder\/Failure"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Type-Aliases","title":"Type Aliases"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeBatchEncoder\/batchLimit"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Type-Properties","title":"Type Properties"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding"]]},"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AmplitudeBatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"overview","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Make the destination with ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/amplitude(apiKey:region:plan:backoff:clock:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"which fills in the endpoint, this encoder and Amplitude’s limits:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let amplitude = try HTTPDestination.amplitude(","    apiKey: apiKey,","    region: .eu,  \/\/ or .us, where the project's data resides","    plan: plan)"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The body is a JSON object of content type ","type":"text"},{"code":"application\/json","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with two members: ","type":"text"},{"code":"api_key","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"project’s API key, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"events","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", one object per record, oldest first, with these members:","type":"text"}]},{"header":"row","type":"table","rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Member"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Holds"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"device_id","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The record’s session, its "},{"code":"SessionKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", as a lowercase UUID string; the record’s own "},{"code":"EventRecord\/id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" when its context has no session"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"event_properties","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The event’s stored properties, by name","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"event_type","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The event’s "},{"code":"Event\/name","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", as it is"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"insert_id"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The record’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventRecord\/id"},{"type":"text","text":", as a lowercase UUID string; a redelivered record keeps it"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"session_id","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The session’s start in Unix milliseconds, the first 48 bits of its version 7 "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SessionKey"},{"type":"text","text":"; left out for a record with no session, or a session key of another version"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"time","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"When the event was tracked, in whole milliseconds since 1970","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The session is the only identifier sent: there is no ","type":"text"},{"code":"user_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and no ","type":"text"},{"code":"ip","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"idfv","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or other","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"device identifier. Amplitude counts a user per ","type":"text"},{"code":"device_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so its unique users are sessions. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"record with no session (one tracked by a tracker without ","type":"text"},{"code":"Enricher.sessions()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or one a store","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"recovered after a relaunch, which keeps no context) is its own anonymous user, linked to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"nothing: Amplitude rejects an event with neither a ","type":"text"},{"code":"device_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" nor a ","type":"text"},{"code":"user_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Amplitude drops","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a second copy of an event with the same ","type":"text"},{"code":"insert_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"device_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so a recovered record that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Amplitude had already stored under its session, before the app ended, is stored again. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"record’s vendor identifier and trace context, and any other context value, aren’t sent. Nor is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"an ","type":"text"},{"code":"ip","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": neither an address nor ","type":"text"},{"code":"$remote","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which asks Amplitude to look the user’s location up","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"from the request’s address.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Properties are read through the event’s schema in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"plan"},{"type":"text","text":", as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PropertyReader"},{"type":"text","text":" reads them. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Sensitive"},{"type":"text","text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals: the property is left"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"out, an element of an array is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"null"},{"type":"text","text":", and one inside a type the plan can’t map is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"null"},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Amplitude limits each string value to 1,024 characters; the encoder sends longer ones as they"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each event also holds these members, for each of the keys the record’s context has a value"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for:"}]},{"header":"row","type":"table","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Member","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Key"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Holds","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"app_version"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ApplicationKey"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The version, left out when ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"device_model","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DeviceKey"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The model"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"language","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LocaleKey"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The locale’s BCP 47 identifier, such as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"en-US"},{"type":"text","text":", which Amplitude stores as the language’s name"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"platform"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"os_name"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"os_version"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OperatingSystemKey"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The operating system’s name, its name again, and its version","type":"text"}]}]]]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A record the encoder can’t write is left out of the request, and the batch’s other records are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sent: one whose event and version ","type":"text"},{"code":"plan","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" doesn’t describe, one whose event name Amplitude keeps","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"for its own events, one whose event isn’t ","type":"text"},{"code":"Encodable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", one that holds a value JSON can’t, one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"whose timestamp has no epoch-milliseconds form, and one too large for a request","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeEncodingError","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":"). ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" returns them as ","type":"text"},{"code":"SkippedRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"s, which","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" logs and reports on its ","type":"text"},{"code":"dropReports","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)"},{"type":"text","text":" splits a batch into requests within the encoder’s limit, "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeBatchEncoder\/batchLimit"},{"type":"text","text":" by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"default, and makes none for a batch with no record it can write, so "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" sends"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"nothing for it. Amplitude answers a request it takes with 200, so "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" retries"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one that gets no response, a 5xx, 408 or 429, and drops one it rejects, such as with 400 or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"413. A record sent again keeps its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"insert_id"},{"type":"text","text":". The bytes are the same for the same records on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every run and platform: no whitespace, object members in the order of their names’ UTF-8"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"bytes."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://AmplitudeEncoding/documentation/AmplitudeEncoding/AmplitudeBatchEncoder/Failure":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Why a record was left out of the batch’s requests."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeBatchEncoder\/Failure","title":"AmplitudeBatchEncoder.Failure","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"typealias"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Failure"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Failure"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/